# Committed on purpose — these are NOT credentials.
#
# Vite loads .env.[mode] after .env, and `vite`/`vite dev` default to mode
# "development" — so this is what `pnpm dev` picks up with no flag, pointing
# local dev at the Dockerized local Supabase stack (`pnpm db:start`, run from
# the repo root) instead of production. admin's write-heavy RPCs
# (admin_save_chapter, admin_set_disabled, etc.) are exactly the ones a bad
# migration is most likely to break, so this is the app where dev-hitting-prod
# was riskiest. The key and URL below are the Supabase CLI's fixed local demo
# values — identical on every machine, published in Supabase's own docs, and
# meaningless without also holding a shell on this machine's Docker containers.
#
# To point local dev at something else deliberately (e.g. staging), create
# .env.development.local — Vite loads it after this file and it's gitignored.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_ACJWlzQHlZjBrEguHvfOxg_3BJgxAaH
